endobj
635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (This project presents the design and implementation of a cloud-based Security Operations Center \(SOC\) using Microsoft Azure and Microsoft Sentinel. The purpose of this project is to build a centralized security monitoring environment capable of collecting, analyzing, and responding to cybersecurity events in real time. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
636 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (The implemented system utilizes Microsoft Azure cloud infrastructure to host a Windows Server virtual machine that serves as the primary monitored endpoint. Logs generated from the server are collected using Azure Monitor Agent and forwarded to Log Analytics Workspace, where they are stored and processed. Microsoft Sentinel is integrated as a Security Information and Event Management \(SIEM\) platform to analyze incoming security events, detect suspicious behavior, and generate alerts and incidents. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (The project focuses on simulating real-world cyberattacks, including brute force login attempts and network reconnaissance using Nmap port scanning. Detection rules were created using )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (Kusto Query Language \(KQL\) to identify abnormal patterns and trigger automated responses. Additional monitoring capabilities were enhanced through the installation of Sysmon, which provides detailed system activity logs. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (To improve visibility and usability, dashboards and workbooks were developed to visualize attack trends, suspicious IP addresses, incident statistics, and geographic locations of detected events. Automation workflows were also implemented using Azure Logic Apps to simulate incident response actions such as notifications and alert handling. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 462 0 R
/E (The results demonstrate that the proposed SOC architecture can effectively collect logs, detect attacks, generate incidents, and provide real-time monitoring within a cloud environment. The project highlights the advantages of cloud-native security monitoring solutions, including scalability, flexibility, centralized management, and reduced infrastructure complexity. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
