/T (1.1 Background of the Study )
/E (1.1 Background of the Study )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
992 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E (The rapid evolution of information technology and the widespread adoption of digital services have significantly increased the dependency of organizations on interconnected systems, cloud platforms, and online infrastructure. Businesses, educational institutions, healthcare providers, financial organizations, and government sectors now rely heavily on digital environments to store data, deliver services, and manage operations. While this transformation has improved efficiency and accessibility, it has also introduced a growing number of cybersecurity risks. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
993 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E (Cyber threats have become increasingly advanced, frequent, and difficult to detect using traditional security solutions. Attackers continuously develop new methods to exploit vulnerabilities, compromise systems, steal sensitive information, and disrupt business operations. Common cyberattacks include brute force attacks, malware infections, ransomware, phishing campaigns, insider threats, credential theft, denial-of-service attacks, and network reconnaissance activities such as port scanning. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
994 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E (Traditional security monitoring approaches are often fragmented and reactive. Many organizations rely on standalone antivirus software, firewalls, or manual monitoring practices that are insufficient in detecting sophisticated attacks across distributed environments. Security teams require centralized monitoring solutions that can collect logs from multiple systems, correlate events, identify suspicious behavior, and provide real-time incident visibility. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
995 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
996 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E (In recent years, cloud computing has become a major driver in modern cybersecurity operations. Cloud platforms offer flexibility, scalability, centralized management, and reduced hardware dependency. Microsoft Azure is one of the leading cloud service providers that offers integrated security capabilities for building enterprise-grade monitoring environments. Azure provides infrastructure services, monitoring tools, security analytics, networking features, and automation capabilities that can be combined to create a cloud-based SOC. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
997 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E (Microsoft Sentinel is a cloud-native Security Information and Event Management \(SIEM\) and Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response \(SOAR\) platform built within Azure. Sentinel allows organizations to collect logs from multiple sources, perform threat detection using )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
998 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 473 0 R
/Pg 26 0 R
/A [3191 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
999 0 obj
<<
