/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (2 )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1000 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (analytics rules, create incidents, visualize attack patterns, and automate response actions. Since Sentinel operates fully within the cloud, it eliminates the need for complex on-premises infrastructure while maintaining enterprise-level monitoring capabilities. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1001 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (This project focuses on designing and implementing a cloud-based SOC using Microsoft Azure and Microsoft Sentinel. The proposed solution demonstrates how cloud services can be integrated to create a centralized security monitoring environment. The project includes log collection, attack simulation, dashboard visualization, alert generation, incident management, and event analysis. Through this implementation, the project aims to simulate a real-world SOC capable of detecting and responding to cybersecurity activities. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1002 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (Modern organizations generate a large volume of logs and security events every day. These logs originate from user authentication activities, network traffic, system operations, applications, cloud resources, and endpoint devices. Without centralized monitoring, security teams face significant challenges in analyzing this data efficiently. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1003 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (Traditional monitoring methods often rely on isolated tools that provide limited visibility into the overall environment. For example, antivirus solutions may detect malware but cannot correlate network activity or authentication events. Firewalls may block traffic but do not always provide advanced behavioral analytics. This fragmented approach creates security gaps that attackers can exploit. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1004 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (Another challenge is the increasing complexity of cloud environments. As organizations migrate services to the cloud, monitoring becomes more difficult due to distributed resources, dynamic infrastructure, and hybrid networks. Security teams require a unified platform capable of aggregating logs from multiple sources and analyzing them in real time. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1005 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (Additionally, manual security monitoring is time-consuming and inefficient. Analysts may struggle to identify suspicious patterns among thousands of events. Delayed detection can increase the impact of attacks, allowing threat actors to move laterally within a network, escalate privileges, or compromise sensitive information. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1006 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (Many small organizations and academic environments also face limitations related to cost, infrastructure, and technical complexity. Building a traditional on-premises SOC requires expensive hardware, dedicated infrastructure, and specialized personnel. This creates barriers for implementing advanced cybersecurity monitoring. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1007 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (The primary problem addressed in this project is the absence of a centralized, scalable, and cost- effective security monitoring solution capable of detecting cyber threats in real time. The project aims to demonstrate how Microsoft Azure and Microsoft Sentinel can provide an efficient cloud-)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
