1107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/E (Cybersecurity has become one of the most important disciplines in modern information technology due to the rapid increase in cyber threats and the growing dependence on digital infrastructure. Organizations rely heavily on computer networks, cloud systems, remote access services, online databases, and internet-connected applications. As technology evolves, attackers also continue to develop more advanced techniques that target vulnerabilities in systems and networks. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/E (A literature review provides a theoretical understanding of the technologies, concepts, and security practices related to the proposed project. It helps establish a foundation for the research by analyzing previous studies, existing solutions, and current cybersecurity trends. In the context of this project, the literature review focuses on Security Operations Centers \(SOC\), cloud computing, SIEM technologies, Microsoft Sentinel, Azure security services, and existing monitoring solutions. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/E (The purpose of this chapter is to explain the technical background required to understand the development of a cloud-based SOC. The chapter reviews modern cybersecurity monitoring practices and discusses how organizations can benefit from centralized threat detection and incident response platforms. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/E (In recent years, cloud-native security monitoring has become increasingly popular due to its scalability, flexibility, and reduced infrastructure requirements. Organizations are shifting away from traditional security architectures toward cloud-based monitoring solutions that provide real- time visibility into network activity, authentication events, endpoint behavior, and suspicious activity. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 478 0 R
/E (This chapter also highlights how SIEM platforms evolved to support advanced analytics, automated response, and integration with cloud ecosystems. Microsoft Sentinel, as a cloud-native SIEM, plays a major role in enabling organizations to implement modern security operations. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
