/E (Attack simulation and testing represent one of the most important phases in cybersecurity projects because they validate whether the deployed monitoring environment functions correctly under realistic conditions. The purpose of testing is not only to verify that logs are collected successfully, but also to confirm that alerts, incident generation, dashboards, and monitoring workflows behave as expected when suspicious activity occurs. )
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1798 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 510 0 R
/E (In a Security Operations Center \(SOC\), testing plays a critical role in ensuring that security controls are operational. Without attack simulation, the SOC would only exist as a theoretical configuration without practical evidence of effectiveness. )
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
